//! task: fix
//! ask: Get the filesystem capability from an environment capability.
//! expect: EXS-E0305
//! refs: §4.6, §5.2
//! explain: Capabilities are unforgeable, and no `sicut` retypes a value into or out of a capability atom (`EXS-E0305`). Authority is derived from the root `Mundus`, explicitly: `m.archivum()`. A function that was never handed the authority cannot cast its way to it, which is what makes the audit's reading of the interface trustworthy.

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    firma b = a sicut archivum;
    redde 0;
}
//@ fixed
publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    firma b = m.archivum();
    redde 0;
}
